Subject: [PATCH] Hoist the chunk lookup out of the getLightLevel neighbor
 probes

World#c(BlockPosition, boolean) with flag=true (getLightLevel) probes five
neighbors when the block diffuses light, and each probe resolved its chunk
through ChunkProviderServer#getChunkIfLoaded - six map lookups per call
overall, called per candidate position by mob spawning and per burning mob
per tick by the sun-burn checks.

Resolve the center chunk once and share it with the neighbor probes: the
vertical neighbor always stays in the center chunk and the horizontal ones
only cross a border at chunk edges. A shared private tail method keeps the
vanilla semantics exactly: out-of-bounds positions return 15, y<0 returns
0, y>=256 clamps to 255 before the read, and unloaded chunks return 0.

Verified with a 300k-case simulation covering chunk borders, unloaded
neighbor chunks, y clamping and out-of-bounds coordinates: zero divergences
from the vanilla resolution order.

